<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theron of Acragas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 472 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theron of Acragas (died 472 BCE) was tyrant of the Greek city of Acragas in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> from about 488 BCE. He expelled Terillus from Himera around 483 BCE, provoking a Carthaginian invasion, and with his son-in-law <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gelon">Gelon of Syracuse</a> destroyed Hamilcar's army at the Battle of Himera in 480 BCE. His son Thrasydaeus then governed Himera.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/theron-of-acragas.jpg" alt="Theron of Acragas" width="320" height="391" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giuseppe Emanuele Ortolani · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Terone.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
